--TEST--
`delete` and `cancel` are asked the same way and answer the same type, so the "cancel it, or else remove it" idiom is one shape — `rule:concurrency/queue-deletion-is-explicit-and-bounded`, `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The agreement, not either member's own answer: both take one receipt and
// both answer whether *this* call is what took the job out, so a program can
// write the two in sequence without converting anything between them. A member
// that had grown its own comparison would still look right on its own line and
// would fail here.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");
bool $stopped = Core\Queue::cancel($receipt);
bool $removed = Core\Queue::delete($receipt);
bool $either = $stopped || $removed;

// They agree on the arity too: the receipt names both the row and the queue,
// so there is no second argument for either of them to be told which queue to
// look in.
bool $again = Core\Queue::delete($receipt, "email");
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: expected 1 argument(s), found 2
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
